{title: Three Months in Jerusalem}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 23:31–34}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [D7sus4] |
| [D7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]He was twen-ty-three when he took the throne [Dm/F]
[Ebmaj7]His mother Hamutal from Libnah was known
[Cm7]Three short months in Jerusalem he stayed
[D7sus4]Evil in the Lord's sight was the [D7]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pharaoh [Gm]Neco came to take his place
Ri[Dm/F]blah [Ebmaj7]became his prison and his race
A hun[Gm7/D]dred [Cm7]talents of silver and gold
The heavy [D7sus4]weight of the tribute [D7]told
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]He could not reign in Jerusalem's gate [Dm/F]
[Ebmaj7]Imprisoned in the land of Hamath state
[Ebmaj7/D]His [Cm7]brother Eliakim rose to the crown
Je[D7sus4]hoiakim was the name he re[D7]ceived now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pharaoh [Gm]Neco came to take his place
Ri[Dm/F]blah be[Ebmaj7]came his prison and his race
A hun[Ebmaj7/D]dred [Cm7]talents of silver and gold
The heavy [D7sus4]weight of the tribute [D7]told
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]To Egypt he was taken by force [Dm/F]
[Ebmaj7]And there in the distance he found his course [Dm]
[Cm7]Jehoahaz died far from his home
In [D7sus4]the shadow of [D7]the pharaoh's throne
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pharaoh [Gm]Neco came to take his place
Ri[Dm/F]blah be[Ebmaj7]came his prison and his race
A hun[Ebmaj7/D]dred [Cm7]talents of silver and gold
The heavy weight [D7sus4]of the tribute told
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Three months of rule and then the end [Dm/F]
[Ebmaj7]A king displaced by a [D7sus4]foreign [Gm]friend
{end_of_verse}

